From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: tests: TWT teardowns, beacons and BA
 stops on mac80211's own interfaces

The callbacks that hand an interface back to mac80211 had no test: the
main tests' interfaces were the driver's part only, and mac80211 would
look past them for its own. That left the TWT teardowns sent after a
firmware restart (MilkFlint's own code) at 0%, and the beacon a BSS
gives the firmware untested beyond "beaconing off".

The KUnit build gives mt7915/main.c mac80211's internal headers (as tx.c
has them for the power save simulation), and main-test.c an AP interface
that is mac80211's sub_if_data, with a beacon when a test needs one.

- mt7915_main_test_twt_send_teardown: an unprotected S1G TWT Teardown
  with the flow, from the interface, on the voice queue of the station's
  band, counted; one mac80211 drops (a 4-address VLAN without its
  station) neither sent nor counted.
- mt7915_main_test_twt_lost: after a restart each lost flow is torn down
  in turn and counted lost, once.
- mt7915_main_test_add_beacon: mac80211's template (TIM included) in the
  enabled offload TLV; off, none; too large for the firmware, or no
  beacon, refused with nothing sent.
- mt7915_main_test_ampdu_tx_stop_cont: the firmware session ends, the txq
  stops aggregating, mac80211 is told.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/Makefile          |   6 +
 mt7915/tests/main-test.c | 362 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 368 insertions(+)

